# Runtime environment reference. This file is not automatically loaded.
# Optional absolute data directory; default is the OS-local AtrisShare folder.
# PowerShell example: $env:ATRIS_SHARE_DATA_DIR = 'D:\AtrisShareData'
# ATRIS_SHARE_DATA_DIR=
# The desktop generates its own session token and binds 127.0.0.1 on a random port.
# Do not hard-code runtime tokens or change the bind address.
# Google Desktop OAuth fallback (see docs/YOUTUBE.md). Prefer Accounts > YouTube app setup:
# saved locally in the encrypted OS vault, active immediately and persistent after restart.
# Saved local config takes precedence; UI/API never read credentials back or use browser storage.
# ATRIS_SHARE_YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID=<desktop-client-id>.apps.googleusercontent.com
# ATRIS_SHARE_YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET=<desktop-client-secret-if-required>
# These fallback values apply at launch when no saved local config exists; not account tokens.
# Never put real configuration values, account tokens or passwords in this file.
# Optional external media executables; otherwise ffmpeg / ffprobe resolve from PATH.
# ATRIS_SHARE_FFMPEG=
# ATRIS_SHARE_FFPROBE=
# No FFmpeg/FFprobe binary is bundled. Export needs libx264, AAC and caption drawtext.
# Local speech transcription: external whisper.cpp CLI (otherwise whisper-cli on PATH).
# Use an absolute native executable path when setting this override.
# ATRIS_SHARE_WHISPER_CLI=
# Required absolute local path to a compatible whisper.cpp GGML model; no auto-download.
# ATRIS_SHARE_WHISPER_MODEL=
# FFmpeg extracts 16 kHz mono 16-bit PCM; maximum source duration is two hours.
# Speech stays local unless includeTranscript is explicitly enabled for an AI request/MCP grant.
# AI transcript context: <=16,000 text characters / 150 segments; memory is a separate opt-in.
# Optional absolute native OpenCode executable; otherwise safe native discovery is used.
# ATRIS_SHARE_OPENCODE=
# Currently verified OpenCode 1.19.5 only; other versions fail closed. Login stays CLI-owned.
# AtrisShare preserves the CLI auth-store path, never reads/copies its credentials.
# External MCP client environment only: copy actual values/command from the Studio AI UI.
# ATRIS_SHARE_MCP_ORIGIN=
# ATRIS_SHARE_MCP_GRANT=
# Origin must be the running http://127.0.0.1:port without a trailing slash.
# Grant is separate from the desktop bearer, scoped and valid for 30 minutes;
# expiry, UI revocation or runtime restart requires a new grant. Never commit a grant.
# transcript_read requires explicit transcript opt-in; start/status/cancel return no speech text.
# Checkout: npm run build, then npm run mcp:stdio with these variables already set.
# Packaged clients use the actual Node + mcp.mjs command supplied by the UI.
# Live OAuth/AI and all-feature end-to-end acceptance are deferred to Phase 9 (docs/ACCEPTANCE.md).
# No secrets were provided and no live OAuth/inference acceptance is claimed.
